1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,530
If you're a <font color="#00FFFF"><b>mobile engineer</b></font>

2
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:03,190
feeling <font color="#FF5252"><b>intimidated by AI</b></font>

3
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:05,590
thinking you need a <font color="#FF5252"><b>math PhD</b></font>?

4
00:00:05,610 --> 00:00:06,480
Here's the reality:

5
00:00:06,890 --> 00:00:08,670
you already understand most of

6
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:10,290
<font color="#00FFFF"><b>AI serving infrastructure</b></font>.

7
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:13,010
Let me show you exactly which parts.

8
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:14,080
Production AI isn't

9
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,690
calling a <font color="#FF5252"><b>Python API</b></font>.

10
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:18,000
It's an <font color="#00FFFF"><b>operating systems problem</b></font>.

11
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:19,390
Fought Android and iOS

12
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:20,440
<font color="#00FFFF"><b>low-memory killers</b></font>?

13
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:21,800
That's <font color="#00FFFF"><b>preemption</b></font>:

14
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:23,050
when a GPU runs out of

15
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:23,780
<font color="#00FFFF"><b>KV cache</b></font>,

16
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,000
the serving engine <font color="#FF5252"><b>evicts a request</b></font>

17
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:28,100
exactly the way the OS

18
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:29,800
kills your backgrounded app.

19
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:31,450
And <font color="#00FFFF"><b>virtual memory paging</b></font> —

20
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:33,080
the reason your app doesn't crash

21
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:35,170
when it touches more memory than exists —

22
00:00:35,190 --> 00:00:36,850
that's <font color="#00FFFF"><b>PagedAttention</b></font>.

23
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,270
Same page tables,

24
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:40,080
same fix for <font color="#00FFFF"><b>fragmentation</b></font>.

25
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,470
Ever chased a <font color="#00FFFF"><b>16ms frame drop</b></font>

26
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:43,600
on the main thread?

27
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:46,340
Same discipline as <font color="#00FFFF"><b>Time-to-First-Token</b></font>:

28
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:48,640
a hard budget the user can feel,

29
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:51,570
and profiling until you find where it went.

30
00:00:51,590 --> 00:00:53,940
Reactive streams, network drops,

31
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,150
retry state machines?

32
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:56,420
That's <font color="#00FFFF"><b>token streaming</b></font>

33
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:57,860
and <font color="#00FFFF"><b>model fallbacks</b></font>.

34
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,780
And as models move <font color="#00FFFF"><b>on-device</b></font> —

35
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,360
<font color="#00FFFF"><b>ExecuTorch, CoreML, phone NPUs</b></font> —

36
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:04,870
the constraint intuition you've built

37
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:05,600
for <font color="#00FFFF"><b>thirteen years</b></font>

38
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:07,350
becomes the <font color="#00FFFF"><b>advantage</b></font>.

39
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:08,790
Backend folks are the ones

40
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:09,900
<font color="#FF5252"><b>catching up</b></font> here.

41
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,570
What you <font color="#FF5252"><b>don't have yet</b></font>:

42
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:14,860
<font color="#00FFFF"><b>non-deterministic outputs</b></font>, <font color="#00FFFF"><b>embeddings</b></font>,

43
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,010
and <font color="#00FFFF"><b>cost per call</b></font>

44
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:17,470
as a design constraint.

45
00:01:17,490 --> 00:01:18,840
That's the <font color="#FF5252"><b>real gap</b></font> —

46
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:20,090
and it's <font color="#FFD700"><b>learnable</b></font>.

47
00:01:20,110 --> 00:01:22,580
I've built mobile platforms <font color="#00FFFF"><b>since 2013</b></font>

48
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,490
and still lead a mobile team.

49
00:01:24,510 --> 00:01:25,980
<font color="#00FFFF"><b>Same mental models</b></font>.

50
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,560
<font color="#FFD700"><b>Share this</b></font> with a mobile engineer

51
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:28,230
who feels <font color="#FF5252"><b>late</b></font>,

52
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:29,620
grab the <font color="#FFD700"><b>open-source Vault</b></font>

53
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:30,440
in my bio,

54
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:31,800
and <font color="#FFD700"><b>follow @ai.transition</b></font>.
